ent Resources\nGraduate Student Resources\nPre-College Programs\nStudent Experience\nAdvising\nPeer Tutoring & Supplemental Instruction\nStudent Organizations\nStudent Success\nSenior Design Expo\nEngineering Housing\nResearch\nCenter for Energy Systems Research\nCenter for Manufacturing Research\nCybersecurity Education, Research and Outreach Center\nMachine Intelligence and Data Science (MInDS) Research Center\niMakerSpace\nResearch Projects\nFaculty Expertise\nResearch Lab Directory\nEngage\nAlumni\nPartners\nCareers\nGiving\nContact Us\nNews & Events\nNewsroom\nEvents\nWatch Us Grow\nGraduate Studies\nAs the state of Tennessee\u2019s only technological university, Tennessee Tech develops\ninnovative engineers and scholars who solve technological challenges to meet the needs\nof society. We are deeply committed to providing our graduate students with high-level\nresearch and professional development. Whether you are choosing to work in academia\nand need research and teaching opportunities or are pursuing graduate school to take\nyour career to new levels, you will be working closely with supportive, entrepreneurial\nfaculty to solve the problems of tomorrow.\nThe College of Engineering\u2019s graduate programs began five decades ago, and today are\noffered across five departments\u2014including our college-wide Ph.D. program. Administered\njointly with the College of Graduate Studies, our grad programs are large enough to\noffer academic diversity and interdisciplinary challenge, yet small enough to ensure\npersonal attention and rigorous instruction.\nDiscover Graduate Study in the College of Engineering\nMasters\nLearn More\nDoctoral\nLearn More\nResearch\nLearn More\nExperience Tech For Yourself\nVisit us to see what sets us apart.\nSchedule Your Visit\nBack to\nTop\n1 William L Jones Dr\nCookeville, TN 38505\nGeneral Information: (931) 372-3101\nCampus Police: (931) 372-3234\nAdmissions: (931) 372-3888\nDonate\nApply\nVisit\nAdmissions\nAthletics\nNews\nCale